00:11:28.054 --> 00:11:29.837
to my dad's and that was a big mountain

00:11:29.837 --> 00:11:32.354
for an immigrant like
wow, dad did it right?

00:11:32.354 --> 00:11:33.869
If you want to say I'm gonna climb that

00:11:33.869 --> 00:11:36.358
and I'm gonna climb bigger, awesome.

00:11:36.358 --> 00:11:39.082
I'm pumped, I'm weirdly
not cheering for you 'cause

00:11:39.082 --> 00:11:40.261
(man laughs)

00:11:40.261 --> 00:11:41.859
I'm just a weirdly competitive dude.

00:11:41.859 --> 00:11:44.027
This is actually something
I'm not proud of.

00:11:44.027 --> 00:11:45.629
I'm comfortable saying this

00:11:45.629 --> 00:11:47.848
and I believe this is a flaw.

00:11:47.848 --> 00:11:50.212
But I don't want my kids
to beat me, I don't.

00:11:50.212 --> 00:11:51.954
I hate saying it.

00:11:51.954 --> 00:11:54.026
I know this is where I get in trouble.

00:11:54.026 --> 00:11:55.267
People will take one little clip

00:11:55.267 --> 00:11:56.700
from one video interview and they're like,

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.026
"You're bad."

00:11:58.026 --> 00:11:58.859
It's just my truth.

00:11:58.859 --> 00:11:59.944
I don't want to bullshit you guys.

00:11:59.944 --> 00:12:01.608
I'm that competitive.

00:12:01.608 --> 00:12:04.775
(slow dramatic music)

00:12:15.503 --> 00:12:18.842
I just want them to be all in on them.

00:12:18.842 --> 00:12:21.069
I don't need them to be an entrapuener,

00:12:21.069 --> 00:12:22.826
I don't need them to make me proud,

00:12:22.826 --> 00:12:24.278
they don't need to go to Harvard,

00:12:24.278 --> 00:12:25.272
they don't need to do shit.

00:12:25.272 --> 00:12:26.885
They need to be themselves, all in

00:12:26.885 --> 00:12:29.313
and they need to be kind and good.

00:12:29.313 --> 00:12:32.480
(slow dramatic music)

00:12:34.288 --> 00:12:36.624
Everybody thinks they're stuff is so good.

00:12:36.624 --> 00:12:39.977
Every day Gary, my Instagram's so on fire.

00:12:39.977 --> 00:12:41.310
It's so awesome.

00:12:43.355 --> 00:12:45.159
Why am I not gaining followers?

00:12:45.159 --> 00:12:47.159
'Cause it's not awesome.

00:12:49.309 --> 00:12:51.952
Think, we all think our stuff is the best.

00:12:51.952 --> 00:12:53.046
I get that.

00:12:53.046 --> 00:12:54.573
But yeah, that would be my advise.

00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:57.267
Only because that, also, is liberating.

00:12:57.267 --> 00:12:59.763
To me, everything's about breathing.

00:12:59.763 --> 00:13:01.530
To me, everything is about take

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.777
full ownership for everything.

00:13:03.777 --> 00:13:04.889
And then everything gets easy.

00:13:04.889 --> 00:13:07.091
'Cause then you're in control.

00:13:07.091 --> 00:13:08.972
And then learn how to love to lose.

00:13:08.972 --> 00:13:11.278
I think that's how entrepreneurship,

00:13:11.278 --> 00:13:12.176
that's how life is.

00:13:12.176 --> 00:13:13.676
We all have loses.

00:13:14.689 --> 00:13:16.815
I like loses. I love adversity.

00:13:16.815 --> 00:13:18.231
I like the climb.

00:13:18.231 --> 00:13:19.806
I like the chip on my shoulder.

00:13:19.806 --> 00:13:21.478
I like when people are
like, "Oh I knew it."

00:13:21.478 --> 00:13:23.403
"He's not that good."

00:13:23.403 --> 00:13:25.697
I'm even weirdly scared as I continue

00:13:25.697 --> 00:13:27.607
to ascend and I'm getting popular

00:13:27.607 --> 00:13:29.216
and what did he say?

00:13:29.216 --> 00:13:30.907
The marketing leaning,
people start putting

00:13:30.907 --> 00:13:32.279
these words in front of my name.

00:13:32.279 --> 00:13:37.269
I'm like, am I gonna sabotage
myself to re correct this?

00:13:37.269 --> 00:13:38.686
I like adversity.

00:13:40.237 --> 00:13:41.570
Yeah, all on me.

00:13:42.986 --> 00:13:44.400
I enjoy loses.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.758
Now, all of a sudden, like what?

00:13:45.758 --> 00:13:47.385
You become completely invincible.

00:13:47.385 --> 00:13:48.265
I feel invincible.

00:13:48.265 --> 00:13:50.812
I really, genuinely, outside of the health

00:13:50.812 --> 00:13:54.979
of myself and 20 people feel
100% invisible as a person.

00:13:56.758 --> 00:13:58.439
I know what my intent is.

00:13:58.439 --> 00:14:02.120
I want to do good at
nobody else's expense.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:04.280
I'm far from perfect, we all are.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.243
It's just easy.

00:14:05.243 --> 00:14:06.630
It feels very light to live life.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:07.784
I'm just in a good mood.

00:14:07.784 --> 00:14:10.730
(slow dramatic music)

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.676
Them home but I think modern day parents

00:14:12.676 --> 00:14:14.663
and most parents do not do that.

00:14:14.663 --> 00:14:17.555
I think they focus on
dumb shit like grades.

00:14:17.555 --> 00:14:19.411
Because they are insecure

00:14:19.411 --> 00:14:21.026
and they want to put the bumper sticker

00:14:21.026 --> 00:14:23.861
that their kids went to Stanford.

00:14:23.861 --> 00:14:25.166
It's real fucked up when you really

00:14:25.166 --> 00:14:27.890
think about what's actually happening.

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:30.133
So much of it is misery loves company.

00:14:30.133 --> 00:14:32.521
Or people reflecting of
what's inside of them.

00:14:32.521 --> 00:14:35.688
(slow dramatic music)

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.563
- What is the impact that you want

00:14:43.563 --> 00:14:45.313
to have on the world?

00:14:46.921 --> 00:14:50.255
- Same thing that attracts so many

00:14:50.255 --> 00:14:52.916
of millions of people to people

00:14:52.916 --> 00:14:54.509
that are selling bullshit.

00:14:54.509 --> 00:14:57.329
Those same people are attracted to me.

00:14:57.329 --> 00:14:59.683
And what I want to do is suffocate out

00:14:59.683 --> 00:15:00.736
all those other people

00:15:00.736 --> 00:15:03.728
and become the alpha of that entire world

00:15:03.728 --> 00:15:07.311
of people that are
hoping and are desperate

00:15:08.471 --> 00:15:10.431
to look at me and what I want to do

00:15:10.431 --> 00:15:12.943
is inspire two 14 year old girls

00:15:12.943 --> 00:15:14.647
in Kansas City, right now,

00:15:14.647 --> 00:15:16.801
to build a billion dollar company

00:15:16.801 --> 00:15:18.069
on having a bunch of employees

00:15:18.069 --> 00:15:20.003
hugging each other in the halls.

00:15:20.003 --> 00:15:22.509
I think that Steve Jobs came along,

00:15:22.509 --> 00:15:25.720
became an icon but the sad part

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.231
of that narrative was he did not

00:15:27.231 --> 00:15:28.970
treat his employees well.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.089
He became an icon and the narrative became

00:15:31.089 --> 00:15:32.677
he got the most out of people

00:15:32.677 --> 00:15:35.889
by being a jerk and that
became romanticized.

00:15:35.889 --> 00:15:37.980
And a lot of people in
Silicone Valley today,

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.800
run companies where they're mean

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.438
because they think that's
the right thing to do

00:15:41.438 --> 00:15:43.616
because they put Steve Jobs on a pedestal.

00:15:43.616 --> 00:15:45.273
I want my pedestal moment.

00:15:45.273 --> 00:15:46.916
I want to become that big

00:15:46.916 --> 00:15:48.770
and what I want to come from that

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:51.141
is that kids that aren't even born today,

00:15:51.141 --> 00:15:53.946
think that they can build a
five billion dollar company

00:15:53.946 --> 00:15:56.399
and be a great guy or a great gal.

00:15:56.399 --> 00:15:59.803
I want to build the biggest
building in town, ever,

00:15:59.803 --> 00:16:02.018
by just building the
biggest building in town.

00:16:02.018 --> 00:16:03.501
While I think most people try to tear

00:16:03.501 --> 00:16:05.354
down everybody else's building.

00:16:05.354 --> 00:16:08.491
So I think positivity and good

00:16:08.491 --> 00:16:11.039
is practical advise to building an empire

00:16:11.039 --> 00:16:12.365
and I want to be the poster child

00:16:12.365 --> 00:16:14.039
of the person that built the biggest,

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:17.506
baddest, empire and did it by being

00:16:17.506 --> 00:16:19.553
a good dude along the way.

00:16:19.553 --> 00:16:21.062
And not everybody's gonna be happy

00:16:21.062 --> 00:16:22.426
about everything that I did

00:16:22.426 --> 00:16:25.033
but if it's 97% of people talking good

00:16:25.033 --> 00:16:27.406
behind your back, that's a real legacy.

00:16:27.406 --> 00:16:29.751
And I want to do it in a pop culture way.

00:16:29.751 --> 00:16:30.584
I'm gonna do it anyway.

00:16:30.584 --> 00:16:31.534
People have done that before.

00:16:31.534 --> 00:16:32.995
Just so you know,
there's plenty of people.

00:16:32.995 --> 00:16:35.537
Warren Buffet's a really good dude.

00:16:35.537 --> 00:16:38.122
There's plenty of people
that have done that.

00:16:38.122 --> 00:16:39.117
There's a difference.

00:16:39.117 --> 00:16:41.553
I want to do it and I
want to be a rock star.

00:16:41.553 --> 00:16:45.259
And that's where you influence people.

00:16:45.259 --> 00:16:46.850
I want to do it but I also want

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.511
to be the most popular.

00:16:48.511 --> 00:16:49.732
And so then that person's like,

00:16:49.732 --> 00:16:53.430
I want to be him so I guess I'll be nice.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:54.804
I want to literally take people

00:16:54.804 --> 00:16:57.158
who have DNA that's kind of nice

00:16:57.158 --> 00:16:58.863
and make them more nice because

00:16:58.863 --> 00:17:01.909
they think that's how I became big.

00:17:01.909 --> 00:17:03.954
So I basically want to trick

00:17:03.954 --> 00:17:06.679
the business world into becoming kinder.

00:17:06.679 --> 00:17:09.846
(slow dramatic music)

